IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sfa-core`
IMPORT `sfaa-div1-penalties-court`

-- Tests for sfaa-div1-penalties-court.l4 (sections 137D and 137E). Every expected value is written from the text, beside the assertion.


§ `s 137D(1): intentional or reckless contravention, or knowingly false information (split site (i), both readings)`
-- intentional contravention of one of the named sections: guilty
#ASSERT `s 137D(1) the person is guilty of an offence under subsection (1)` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- knowingly false information in purported compliance: guilty
#ASSERT `s 137D(1) the person is guilty of an offence under subsection (1)` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a contravention that is not intentional or reckless: not covered by subsection (1), which says who is guilty and not who is innocent
#ASSERT `s 137D(1) the person is guilty of an offence under subsection (1)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- false information the person did not know to be false: not covered by subsection (1)
#ASSERT `s 137D(1) the person is guilty of an offence under subsection (1)` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 137D(1) the person is guilty of an offence under subsection (1)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the penalty: an individual and a corporation
#ASSERT `s 137D(1) the penalty on conviction` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST (Penalty OF 250000, 24, TRUE, 25000)
#ASSERT `s 137D(1) the penalty on conviction` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST (Penalty OF 250000, 0, FALSE, 25000)
-- neither: the paragraphs name only those two cases
#ASSERT `s 137D(1) the penalty on conviction` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 137D(2): the lesser offence`
-- a contravention that is not intentional or reckless
#ASSERT `s 137D(2) the person is guilty of an offence under subsection (2)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- false or misleading information without the knowledge or recklessness of subsection (1)
#ASSERT `s 137D(2) the person is guilty of an offence under subsection (2)` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- an intentional contravention is within subsection (1) and carved out of this one ("in circumstances other than as set out in subsection (1)")
#ASSERT `s 137D(2) the person is guilty of an offence under subsection (2)` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- no contravention and no false information: not covered
#ASSERT `s 137D(2) the person is guilty of an offence under subsection (2)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 137D(2) the penalty on conviction` EQUALS Penalty OF 25000, 0, FALSE, 2500

§ `s 137D(3): the bar on proceedings`
#ASSERT `s 137D(3) no proceedings may be instituted for an offence under section 137D` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 137D(3) no proceedings may be instituted for an offence under section 137D` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- outside both triggers the bar does not apply (marginal reading (b))
#ASSERT `s 137D(3) no proceedings may be instituted for an offence under section 137D` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 137E(1) to (5): the court's powers`
-- the three conditions of subsection (1) (split site (ii), both readings): all met, the power; any one missing, not covered
#ASSERT `s 137E(1) the court has power to make one or more of the orders listed in the subsection` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 137E(1) the court has power to make one or more of the orders listed in the subsection` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 137E(1) the court has power to make one or more of the orders listed in the subsection` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 137E(1) the court has power to make one or more of the orders listed in the subsection` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 137E(2) the order may include ancillary or consequential provisions the court thinks just` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 137E(2) the order may include ancillary or consequential provisions the court thinks just` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- a sale order carrying the condition, and a buyer who is or would become a substantial shareholder: the sale is barred
#ASSERT `s 137E(3) the sale to the buyer is barred by the court's condition` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 137E(3) the sale to the buyer is barred by the court's condition` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 137E(3) the sale to the buyer is barred by the court's condition` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 137E(3) the sale to the buyer is barred by the court's condition` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (4), split site (ii), both readings
#ASSERT `s 137E(4) the Authority may apply to the court for directions on the unsold share` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 137E(4) the Authority may apply to the court for directions on the unsold share` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 137E(5) the court must first satisfy itself that the order would not unfairly prejudice any person` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 137E(5) the court must first satisfy itself that the order would not unfairly prejudice any person` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 137E(6): when the court is not to make an order`
-- inadvertence and the failure ought to be excused: the court is not to make (most) orders
#ASSERT `s 137E(6) the court is not to make the order` `s 137E(1)(a) an order restraining the substantial shareholder from disposing of any interest in the shares` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 137E(6) the court is not to make the order` `s 137E(1)(e) an order directing the sale of any or all of the shares` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the carve-out "other than an order restraining the exercise of voting rights": paragraph (c) is not barred
#ASSERT `s 137E(6) the court is not to make the order` `s 137E(1)(c) an order restraining the exercise by any person of any voting or other rights attached to a share` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- fork register A7: an order that the exercise of voting rights be disregarded is not "an order restraining" it, so it is barred
#ASSERT `s 137E(6) the court is not to make the order` `s 137E(1)(h) an order that any exercise of the voting or other rights attached to shares be disregarded` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- either condition missing: the "if" is not met, the text's no (marginal reading (a))
#ASSERT `s 137E(6) the court is not to make the order` `s 137E(1)(a) an order restraining the substantial shareholder from disposing of any interest in the shares` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 137E(6) the court is not to make the order` `s 137E(1)(a) an order restraining the substantial shareholder from disposing of any interest in the shares` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 137E(7) to (10): notice, rescission, contravention and contempt`
#ASSERT `s 137E(7) the court may direct that notice of the application be given or published` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 137E(7) the court may direct that notice of the application be given or published` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 137E(8) the court may rescind, vary, discharge or suspend the order` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 137E(8) the court may rescind, vary, discharge or suspend the order` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 137E(9) the person is guilty of an offence of contravening an order of the court` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 137E(9) the person is guilty of an offence of contravening an order of the court` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 137E(9) the penalty on conviction` EQUALS Penalty OF 50000, 0, FALSE, 5000
#ASSERT `s 137E(10) subsection (9) does not affect the court's powers in relation to the punishment of contempt` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 137E(10) subsection (9) does not affect the court's powers in relation to the punishment of contempt` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the prohibition as a rule: contravening the order is a breach; doing nothing leaves the rule standing
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 137E(9) the person shall not contravene an order of the court` (Individual "the person") AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Individual "the person" DOES `s 137E contravene an order of the court made under the section` AT 1
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 137E(9) the person shall not contravene an order of the court` (Individual "the person") AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 5)
